Blackdrift: point privacy, terms, help and support links at sonicon.org.

Why: Focus links to Mozilla's privacy notice, terms of use, SUMO help
articles and manifesto, which describe Mozilla's product, not Blackdrift. All of
them live in SupportUtils, so one file changes:
privacy -> https://sonicon.org/privacy-policy.html,
terms -> https://sonicon.org/terms.html, and help, SUMO topics, safe browsing,
default-browser help and the About "Learn more" -> https://sonicon.org.
getMozillaPageUrl drops its unused locale parameter (no caller passes one);
the SUMO helpers keep their parameters so their call sites need no patch.
The now-unused locale and URL-encoding helpers and imports are removed.
RATE_APP_URL/FOCUS_PLAY_STORE_URL already resolve to Blackdrift's own application
ID; OPEN_WITH_DEFAULT_BROWSER_URL is an internal marker, never loaded.
Focus 159 has no "What's new" link (checked again on 159.0.1).

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

